# SECTION 2 — SERVICE DEFINITION AND BUSINESS RULES

Create a dedicated service called:

**RideNova Parcel — Door-to-Door Delivery**

Tagline: “Pick Up. Track. Deliver. Verify.”

The service allows a customer to send a permitted parcel from one address to another.

The core process is:

1. Customer enters parcel details.
2. Customer uploads parcel photographs.
3. Customer enters pickup and recipient addresses.
4. Backend calculates the delivery fare.
5. Customer chooses online prepaid or cash at pickup.
6. The request is saved to the database.
7. Eligible drivers receive the delivery request.
8. One eligible driver accepts the request.
9. Driver travels to the pickup location.
10. Sender provides a pickup OTP.
11. Driver verifies the pickup OTP and captures pickup evidence.
12. The parcel is recorded as collected.
13. Driver starts the delivery journey.
14. Customer can track the delivery and view persistent details.
15. Driver reaches the destination.
16. Recipient provides a separate delivery OTP.
17. Driver captures delivery evidence.
18. Backend verifies all required completion conditions.
19. Delivery is marked delivered.
20. Customer receives a receipt and can access the completed delivery history.
21. Driver earnings and payment records are updated correctly.

The feature must support these two initial payment methods:

A. ONLINE PREPAID
- Customer pays before the parcel is dispatched.
- Dispatch must not proceed as a prepaid job until payment is authoritatively confirmed by the payment provider and backend.

B. CASH AT PICKUP
- The driver collects the configured delivery fee from the sender at pickup.
- The driver must record the collection.
- The sender must receive an acknowledgement.
- The parcel cannot proceed until the cash-collection requirements are satisfied.
- Do not also charge the same delivery fee online.

Do not implement cash on delivery in this first release. Keep the architecture extensible so it can be added later.

Use separate pickup and delivery OTPs.

Pickup OTP confirms authorised handover by the sender. Delivery OTP confirms handover to the intended recipient.

Do not reuse passenger-ride OTPs or passenger-ride status transitions in a way that breaks the existing ride system.

